Z||000004||turbo86se||09-11-2001||05:38 PM||||My roommate just got home early this morning from her trip to NY to visit family. Before I left for my night classes she showed me several pictures of the WTC taken just yesterday. I can't believe this has happened. <BR>Just the other night my sorta g/f and I were at Friday's having a couple beers talking about whether or not to bring a child into this world. I'm all for it, my sister just gave birth to a beautiful 7lbs girl last Thursday (I'm an uncle  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">). Now I'm thinking otherwise.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sour Lemon||09-11-2001||08:36 PM||||I'm not from the city, but I'm about 40 miles from it.  My mothers boyfriend just went in today to the Mexican Embassy(6 blocks from WTC)He just got home and told us all that there was ash all over the place, and while the buildings were still standing, people were jumping from the burning floors.  He saw the buildings fall.Everyone here is pretty shaken up.  Nothing much else to saw about this terrorist act.||||reg||9
Z||000006||8Ball||09-11-2001||09:12 PM||||Well I have a cousin who works(ed) in the wtc on the 95th floor of the south building.<BR>All we know atm is he always got to the office no later than 8am and was at work today. No one has heard from him and we fear the worst. But all we can do know is wait and hope.<P>Randy||||reg||1
