Z||000013||8Ball||09-12-2001||06:38 PM||||Well the saying goes, No news is good news.<BR>But in this case I would have to say the opposite. No one has heard from him so he is assumed te be no longer with us. We are going to be haveing a memorial service here for him for our family in this part of this country to attend. We hate to assume this so soon but to be honest, if no one has heard anything by now then there is really no chance that he is still alive. From what I hear his mom is still hopeing, but at the same time she is starting to get some form of funeral arrangements together. He will be missed, and was always deeply loved by his family. He was my favorite cousin and one of my favorite family members. I want to thank you all again for being here for me. It is times like this that show all of us just how tite knit this community is. But as it stands Craig Cooper a very beloved member of our family, is just one of thousands of casualities in this most horrific act of war against our nation and against our very way or life.<P>Thank you all again,<BR>Randy Walker||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||09-12-2001||06:46 PM||||Terribly sorry. I don't know what else to say. <BR>You and your family will be in my prayers.<P>Steve <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000015||TI_3VOM||09-12-2001||06:52 PM||||8Ball,<BR>    I kinda know how you feel. I lost my mother 3 weeks ago. She was to recieve a heart valve replacement, and her doctor was the same one that did her bypass 3 years ago. No one saw it coming, and it took all of us by surprise. We all miss her. I'm sure your family's grief is as deep as ours was. My prayers are with you, as well as all in New York and at the Pentagon.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fierochic88||09-12-2001||07:00 PM||||Don't give up hope yet.  They just pulled out a guy who was on the 80th floor when the building collapsed and supposedly he will be okay!<P>Jennifer||||reg||1
Z||000017||Denny||09-12-2001||08:42 PM||||I, like many, really don't know what to say at times like this.  Having suffered losses this year, and in the past, I know that there are no words to ease the pain.<P>Many of us are suffering emotional pain in the form of sadness, frustration, helplessness, and anger.<P>All I can offer is try to remember the good times, the joy you've experienced with him.  And that he'd want your life to go on.<P>Denny Lambert<p>[This message has been edited by Denny (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000018||MsBeth||09-12-2001||09:21 PM||||8ball you family is in our prayers ...so very very sorry  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><BR>MsBeth||||reg||9
Z||000019||Jay||09-12-2001||10:24 PM||||My wife's cousin works right across from the twin towers.  He was in his office when the first plane hit and watched the second one crash into the other tower.  He ran like hell to another building further down the street.  Security guards tried to tell him he couldn't go inside but he forced his way in.  I guess they didn't realize what was going on.  A few minutes later that building was evaquated and they all ran away from the clouds of smoke and debris.  After getting clear of danger he was offered a ride out of Manhatten to his home in New Jersey.  People have been extremely helpful in this time.  It's a relief to know he's okay, and I can really feel for those who are missing.  I've been glued to my TV for the past two days unable to turn away and yet I can't stomach anymore.  This is indeed the story of  our generation.  My sincere hope that some will be found alive.  The will to live is strong.||||reg||1
